# spec_id: eravos.organism.fx-moddelay · version 1.0.0 · phase P8.1 · status canonical
# source: v10 plugins/chorus.json + flanger.json (shells, F-19) · inherits STD.fx
identity:
  id: eravos.fx-moddelay ; label: Mod Delay ; icon: ≋ ; accent: "#33ddff"
  comp_intent: Thicken and swirl a sound — chorus for width, flanger for jet sweeps.
  novelty: Only FX built on LFO-modulated short delay lines; chorus and flanger are the same circuit at different delay ranges (as in hardware).
engine:
  voices: 3 delay lines (chorus) or 1 with feedback (flanger); each DelayNode modulated by its own LFO (phases 0/120/240°)
  chorus: base 7–25 ms, depth ±0.5–8 ms, no feedback, voices panned L/C/R
  flanger: base 0.2–8 ms, depth to 100%, feedback −0.95..0.95 (negative = hollow), through-zero off
  tempo: rate Hz or division sync (1/1…1/16)
config: mode [chorus, flanger] def chorus ; rate 0.02..10 Hz def 0.6 ; sync bool ; div ; depth 0..1 def 0.5 ; base 0.2..25 ms ; feedback −0.95..0.95 ; spread 0..1 def 0.8 ; STD mix
presets (from chorus.json/flanger.json): Juno Wide, Slow Shimmer, Jet Flange, Metallic Neg, Tempo Sweep 1/2
hooks: STD.fx ; mfx.hook.mod_rate STD.mod_in(rate) ; mod_depth STD.mod_in(depth)
ui: hero = delay-time trace per voice (analyser of LFO taps) ; mode segmented ; knobs
tests: STD.fx tests ; flanger base 1 ms fb 0.9 → comb peaks at k·1 kHz ; chorus width: L/R correlation < 0.9 at spread 1

